4
00:00:25,020 --> 00:00:26,440
Can I go with you?

5
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:29,820
I forgot to bring my umbrella.

6
00:00:30,670 --> 00:00:32,200
If I say you can't,

7
00:00:32,730 --> 00:00:34,000
will you go away?

8
00:00:48,980 --> 00:00:50,100
Why are you teasing me like that?

9
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:52,520
I'm just kidding.

10
00:00:56,130 --> 00:00:57,400
I want you to know

11
00:00:58,010 --> 00:00:59,790
that I didn't want you to go far away.

12
00:01:10,410 --> 00:01:11,410
At last,

13
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:15,290
I finally get to see the girl
under the yellow umbrella

14
00:01:15,310 --> 00:01:17,300
I've always dreamt of.

15
00:01:25,240 --> 00:01:28,810
[North Star Entertainment]

16
00:01:30,700 --> 00:01:32,700
[Presents]

17
00:01:33,540 --> 00:01:36,600
[Third Person]

18
00:01:38,800 --> 00:01:48,130
♫The rain keeps splashing beneath our cover,♫

19
00:01:48,680 --> 00:01:53,810
♫Once it was a special place for two lovers♫

20
00:01:53,840 --> 00:01:57,450
♫There was never enough room for the third♫

21
00:01:58,180 --> 00:02:03,870
♫Now, the rain soaks our hearts together♫

22
00:02:03,890 --> 00:02:13,320
♫The question that's trapped in my heart♫

23
00:02:13,720 --> 00:02:18,770
♫Maybe it's time for you to do your part♫

24
00:02:18,790 --> 00:02:23,070
♫Choose the one your heart truly desires♫

25
00:02:23,090 --> 00:02:32,010
♫Before the last raindrop falls,
don't make me shed another tear♫

26
00:02:32,480 --> 00:02:40,610
♫Before the last raindrop falls,
don't make me shed another tear♫

27
00:03:51,970 --> 00:03:53,200
Can I go with you?

28
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:55,110
I forgot to bring my umbrella.

29
00:04:02,130 --> 00:04:03,020
Thank you

30
00:04:03,180 --> 00:04:04,400
for letting me go with you.

31
00:04:35,600 --> 00:04:38,490
Ever since I lost my memories
four years ago,

32
00:04:39,250 --> 00:04:41,690
I've dreamt of the time I fell in love.

33
00:04:43,200 --> 00:04:46,490
I don't know if it's
a memory or just my imagination.

34
00:04:47,150 --> 00:04:48,820
But the dream world

35
00:04:49,290 --> 00:04:51,110
is more interesting than reality.

36
00:05:04,610 --> 00:05:05,610
Kiiro,

37
00:05:06,300 --> 00:05:07,300
aren't you bored

38
00:05:08,010 --> 00:05:10,300
of eating the same food

39
00:05:10,630 --> 00:05:11,990
and staying in the same place every day?

40
00:05:18,180 --> 00:05:19,180
What am I even asking?

41
00:05:20,060 --> 00:05:21,720
What choice do you have?

42
00:05:25,800 --> 00:05:26,800
But it's alright,

43
00:05:26,900 --> 00:05:28,900
you aren't stuck here alone.

44
00:05:31,020 --> 00:05:32,020
I'm stuck here too.

45
00:05:40,580 --> 00:05:41,410
Whatever.

46
00:05:41,990 --> 00:05:43,400
We don't have a choice anyway.

47
00:06:02,250 --> 00:06:04,610
Others might run to exercise,

48
00:06:04,630 --> 00:06:06,170
to focus,

49
00:06:06,190 --> 00:06:07,680
or to compete.

50
00:06:07,700 --> 00:06:10,240
But I run because I don't know what else to do.

51
00:06:10,260 --> 00:06:12,160
I run to pass the time

52
00:06:12,490 --> 00:06:14,200
so that I can go back to sleep and dream.

53
00:07:00,270 --> 00:07:01,470
I never thought...

54
00:07:01,490 --> 00:07:03,600
my dream would be right in front of me.

55
00:07:16,220 --> 00:07:17,120
Is that all?

56
00:07:17,820 --> 00:07:19,210
Are there any apples missing?

57
00:07:20,880 --> 00:07:22,490
Better not go missing again.

58
00:07:27,870 --> 00:07:28,690
I mean...

59
00:07:28,900 --> 00:07:29,900
the apples.

60
00:07:32,790 --> 00:07:34,720
Without your help,

61
00:07:34,980 --> 00:07:36,410
it might've been a lot harder for me.

62
00:07:37,310 --> 00:07:38,810
Thank you so much.

63
00:07:39,600 --> 00:07:40,600
It's alright.

64
00:07:40,830 --> 00:07:41,790
No trouble at all.

65
00:07:45,040 --> 00:07:46,600
Let me help you, too.

66
00:07:54,230 --> 00:07:55,230
Then...

67
00:07:57,570 --> 00:07:58,910
Can I go with you?

68
00:08:04,330 --> 00:08:05,330
Of course,

69
00:08:05,350 --> 00:08:06,890
wherever you're going,

70
00:08:07,110 --> 00:08:08,400
I'll take you there.

71
00:08:15,660 --> 00:08:17,600
I also don't want you to get wet.

72
00:08:19,540 --> 00:08:21,090
Then...

73
00:08:30,800 --> 00:08:31,900
Why is...

74
00:08:32,690 --> 00:08:36,280
the world suddenly less dull?

75
00:08:40,640 --> 00:08:42,400
I think the rain has stopped.

76
00:08:48,110 --> 00:08:48,940
Thank you

77
00:08:48,960 --> 00:08:50,400
for walking with me this far.

78
00:08:52,620 --> 00:08:54,410
Please... excuse me.

79
00:08:57,530 --> 00:08:58,490
Here.

80
00:09:08,870 --> 00:09:09,400
Oh!

81
00:09:19,200 --> 00:09:20,390
Are you alright?

82
00:09:22,690 --> 00:09:24,110
I should be asking you that.

83
00:09:32,960 --> 00:09:34,810
[Emergency Room]

84
00:09:37,260 --> 00:09:39,560
Please collect your medicine that way.

85
00:09:39,580 --> 00:09:40,690
- Thank you.
- Yes.

86
00:09:45,760 --> 00:09:48,100
She's the owner of that flowerpot.

87
00:09:49,020 --> 00:09:49,510
Well...

88
00:09:49,690 --> 00:09:50,790
you seem fine now.

89
00:09:51,270 --> 00:09:52,390
I'll leave then.

90
00:09:52,510 --> 00:09:54,000
What a waste of time.

91
00:09:54,150 --> 00:09:55,300
Hey,

92
00:09:55,430 --> 00:09:57,640
aren't you going to take
responsibility for hurting her?

93
00:09:57,710 --> 00:09:59,240
And who told you to walk around there?

94
00:09:59,910 --> 00:10:01,010
How was I supposed to know

95
00:10:01,140 --> 00:10:03,000
someone would be walking by?

96
00:10:03,310 --> 00:10:05,610
And you think it's okay to
throw a flowerpot like that?

97
00:10:06,240 --> 00:10:07,520
It's my flowerpot.

98
00:10:07,620 --> 00:10:09,020
Whatever I do with it
is none of your business!

99
00:10:09,190 --> 00:10:10,420
But you threw it at a person!

100
00:10:10,440 --> 00:10:11,330
Then why were you walking there?!

101
00:10:11,350 --> 00:10:12,420
Please stop.

102
00:10:13,290 --> 00:10:14,920
I'm fine...

103
00:10:16,890 --> 00:10:17,610
See?

104
00:10:18,060 --> 00:10:19,890
She said she's fine.

105
00:10:20,290 --> 00:10:21,810
So stop sticking your nose in.

106
00:10:23,920 --> 00:10:25,810
I'm really okay now.

107
00:10:26,750 --> 00:10:28,210
Let's go to the police station.

108
00:10:29,060 --> 00:10:30,420
Let the police handle this.

109
00:10:37,320 --> 00:10:39,310
I thought you'd be angrier,

110
00:10:39,710 --> 00:10:40,200
but...

111
00:10:40,220 --> 00:10:42,920
you asked for the flowerpot
that fell on you as compensation?

112
00:10:43,470 --> 00:10:45,280
Don't you want compensation
for wasting your time?

113
00:10:47,190 --> 00:10:48,190
What about you?

114
00:10:48,640 --> 00:10:49,510
Hm?

115
00:10:50,380 --> 00:10:52,400
You're the one whose time was wasted

116
00:10:52,490 --> 00:10:53,710
because you helped me.

117
00:10:55,510 --> 00:10:57,510
You are the one helping me.

118
00:10:57,620 --> 00:10:58,710
Without you,

119
00:10:58,830 --> 00:11:00,310
I would've gotten injured.

120
00:11:01,190 --> 00:11:02,310
Then that's alright.

121
00:11:04,640 --> 00:11:06,400
We helped each other out.

122
00:11:08,940 --> 00:11:10,720
And this plant, too.

123
00:11:11,840 --> 00:11:13,590
It's not even dead yet.

124
00:11:13,910 --> 00:11:15,190
But she threw it away?

125
00:11:16,840 --> 00:11:19,010
From the looks of it, it might not survive.

126
00:11:19,590 --> 00:11:21,390
I don't even know what plant this is.

127
00:11:22,990 --> 00:11:24,410
It's a rose plant.

128
00:11:24,800 --> 00:11:26,270
If it survives...

129
00:11:26,550 --> 00:11:28,790
The flowers would be beautiful.

130
00:11:32,520 --> 00:11:35,000
You want roses that much?

131
00:11:38,450 --> 00:11:39,900
I want another chance.

132
00:11:44,570 --> 00:11:46,300
Everyone who has made mistakes

133
00:11:46,560 --> 00:11:47,990
would probably want another chance.

134
00:11:48,480 --> 00:11:50,500
If they're sorry

135
00:11:51,210 --> 00:11:52,390
and have already apologized,

136
00:11:53,880 --> 00:11:56,000
I'm willing to forgive them.

137
00:11:58,780 --> 00:12:00,110
How kind of you.

138
00:12:01,790 --> 00:12:02,790
Not really.

139
00:12:05,270 --> 00:12:07,320
I wanted another chance as well.

140
00:12:10,060 --> 00:12:11,300
Both me...

141
00:12:12,880 --> 00:12:13,880
and the rose.

142
00:12:17,930 --> 00:12:19,110
How sad...

143
00:12:20,040 --> 00:12:22,090
I couldn't understand anything you said.

144
00:12:23,870 --> 00:12:25,800
Then would you like to listen a little longer?

145
00:12:28,490 --> 00:12:30,590
My condo isn't far from here,

146
00:12:31,280 --> 00:12:33,590
so can you bring this rose plant...

147
00:12:34,160 --> 00:12:35,900
to its home?

148
00:12:55,980 --> 00:12:57,590
You're... all wet.

149
00:12:57,610 --> 00:12:59,920
Would you like to come inside
to shower and change?

150
00:13:01,920 --> 00:13:02,910
Normally...

151
00:13:02,990 --> 00:13:06,170
do people go into a stranger's room
after meeting them only once?

152
00:13:09,650 --> 00:13:10,800
You're right...

153
00:13:14,410 --> 00:13:15,410
I'm Chris.

154
00:13:16,420 --> 00:13:17,520
What's your name?

155
00:13:18,010 --> 00:13:19,120
I'm Sun.

156
00:13:31,240 --> 00:13:33,000
Nice to meet you, Sun.

157
00:13:34,050 --> 00:13:35,190
I'll be in your care.

158
00:13:36,100 --> 00:13:38,000
Nice to meet you, too.

159
00:13:38,940 --> 00:13:39,720
Chris...

160
00:13:58,320 --> 00:14:00,090
Feel free to use the bathroom.

161
00:14:00,140 --> 00:14:01,300
Wash your hair, too.

162
00:14:01,500 --> 00:14:03,210
Bangkok is full of pollution and dust.

163
00:14:05,580 --> 00:14:06,580
Okay.

164
00:15:33,720 --> 00:15:34,790
Here's some hot cocoa.

165
00:15:34,890 --> 00:15:36,110
It'll help warm you up.

166
00:15:37,710 --> 00:15:38,700
Thank you.

167
00:15:39,710 --> 00:15:41,810
But this is Thailand.

168
00:15:41,890 --> 00:15:44,470
It'll only be cold for a few days
before it gets hot again.

169
00:15:45,710 --> 00:15:46,490
But...

170
00:15:47,200 --> 00:15:48,610
you're shivering.

171
00:15:49,940 --> 00:15:51,900
I'd better drink something warm.

172
00:16:00,720 --> 00:16:02,880
I've never had cocoa like this before.

173
00:16:02,900 --> 00:16:03,900
How did you make this?

174
00:16:03,920 --> 00:16:04,960
It's so delicious.

175
00:16:05,280 --> 00:16:06,280
It's my secret recipe.

176
00:16:06,590 --> 00:16:07,890
If you want to have this,

177
00:16:08,820 --> 00:16:10,430
you can only get it here.

178
00:16:20,820 --> 00:16:22,600
I like your shampoo.

179
00:16:22,750 --> 00:16:24,200
It smells so good.

180
00:16:38,700 --> 00:16:39,900
It actually is.

181
00:16:40,690 --> 00:16:43,080
I like this smell when it's on you, too.

182
00:17:11,480 --> 00:17:12,830
[Nadear]

183
00:17:14,290 --> 00:17:15,210
Ow...

184
00:17:16,080 --> 00:17:16,920
Sun...

185
00:17:17,110 --> 00:17:18,880
I'm sorry. Are you hurt?

186
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:20,000
Let me see.

187
00:17:20,720 --> 00:17:21,530
Whoa.

188
00:17:21,630 --> 00:17:22,730
Does it hurt?

189
00:17:27,220 --> 00:17:28,610
I forgive you.

190
00:17:29,600 --> 00:17:30,690
It's okay.

191
00:17:41,960 --> 00:17:43,560
[Nadear]

192
00:17:47,840 --> 00:17:49,200
Don't you need to head back now?

193
00:17:49,820 --> 00:17:51,100
They're calling you.

194
00:17:55,300 --> 00:17:56,220
Chris,

195
00:17:58,300 --> 00:18:00,510
can I ask you something personal?

196
00:18:03,240 --> 00:18:04,360
What is it?

197
00:18:05,740 --> 00:18:07,310
Do you have a partner?

198
00:18:10,200 --> 00:18:12,070
I... don't have a partner.

199
00:18:38,050 --> 00:18:41,880
[Third Person]

200
00:18:42,958 --> 00:18:46,938
[Third Person]

201
00:19:33,648 --> 00:19:34,738
Chris.

202
00:19:35,748 --> 00:19:36,548
Chris.

203
00:19:37,628 --> 00:19:38,418
Chris?

204
00:19:40,138 --> 00:19:41,048
Chris?

205
00:19:44,288 --> 00:19:46,738
You went quiet after I said
I don't have a partner.

206
00:19:47,138 --> 00:19:48,248
What were you thinking about?

207
00:19:50,278 --> 00:19:52,518
Uh, it's nothing.

208
00:19:54,968 --> 00:19:56,348
Thinking of something lewd, aren't you?

209
00:19:57,018 --> 00:19:58,348
No!

210
00:19:59,548 --> 00:20:01,638
I really wasn't thinking about anything like that.

211
00:20:03,528 --> 00:20:06,008
But your reaction tells me otherwise.

212
00:20:07,048 --> 00:20:07,758
Well,

213
00:20:09,548 --> 00:20:10,548
what were you thinking about?

214
00:20:12,038 --> 00:20:13,138
I want to know your lewd thoughts.

215
00:20:27,838 --> 00:20:28,938
I forgot.

216
00:20:29,558 --> 00:20:30,748
I have a meeting today.

217
00:20:35,088 --> 00:20:35,888
Then...

218
00:20:35,908 --> 00:20:37,148
I won't trouble you any longer.

219
00:20:37,168 --> 00:20:37,948
I'll take my leave.

220
00:20:37,968 --> 00:20:39,348
The rain has stopped as well.

221
00:20:42,928 --> 00:20:43,728
Does that mean...

222
00:20:43,948 --> 00:20:45,438
if I don't have work

223
00:20:45,588 --> 00:20:47,028
and it's still raining,

224
00:20:47,688 --> 00:20:49,248
you're not going to leave?

225
00:20:50,798 --> 00:20:51,648
Yes?

226
00:20:53,608 --> 00:20:54,638
Just kidding.

227
00:20:55,718 --> 00:20:57,058
But this is the first time

228
00:20:57,658 --> 00:20:59,348
I want to skip my meeting,

229
00:20:59,768 --> 00:21:00,628
and...

230
00:21:01,308 --> 00:21:03,128
want it to rain all day.

231
00:21:18,568 --> 00:21:19,558
Take this with you

232
00:21:19,578 --> 00:21:20,628
in case it rains again.

233
00:21:22,448 --> 00:21:23,438
Thank you.

234
00:21:29,148 --> 00:21:29,938
Um...

235
00:21:29,958 --> 00:21:30,958
Sun.

236
00:21:31,938 --> 00:21:32,648
Yes?

237
00:21:34,538 --> 00:21:36,118
Thank you for today.

238
00:21:40,998 --> 00:21:41,788
Then...

239
00:21:41,908 --> 00:21:43,038
please excuse me.

240
00:21:46,668 --> 00:21:48,148
Will you come running again tomorrow?

241
00:21:51,868 --> 00:21:53,828
I usually run every day.

242
00:21:54,818 --> 00:21:55,538
That's great.

243
00:21:55,558 --> 00:21:56,928
I want to run tomorrow as well.

244
00:22:15,748 --> 00:22:17,148
Hello, Kiiro.

245
00:22:17,988 --> 00:22:19,428
You'd definitely be jealous of me

246
00:22:19,448 --> 00:22:21,148
if you knew what happened today.

247
00:22:23,118 --> 00:22:24,448
You're back, Chris?

248
00:22:26,758 --> 00:22:28,038
I called you several times.

249
00:22:28,058 --> 00:22:29,608
Why didn't you answer?

250
00:22:32,058 --> 00:22:33,858
I haven't made a reservation yet.

251
00:22:37,238 --> 00:22:38,438
Where do you think...

252
00:22:39,268 --> 00:22:42,288
we should go celebrate our tenth anniversary?

253
00:22:47,188 --> 00:22:49,048
Do you have a place you want to go?

254
00:22:49,828 --> 00:22:51,158
I'm fine with anywhere.

255
00:22:53,268 --> 00:22:54,648
Pick wherever you like.

256
00:22:57,938 --> 00:22:59,198
You know

257
00:22:59,228 --> 00:23:01,638
there's only one place I like.

258
00:23:04,928 --> 00:23:06,008
Our place.

259
00:23:12,978 --> 00:23:14,708
[Third Person
Bar - Bistro]

260
00:23:14,728 --> 00:23:15,398
Oh, Chris,

261
00:23:15,598 --> 00:23:16,698
long time no see.

262
00:23:16,718 --> 00:23:17,548
Doing well?

263
00:23:18,158 --> 00:23:18,938
Yeah, Nan.

264
00:23:19,038 --> 00:23:20,328
I'm fine, as usual.

265
00:23:20,378 --> 00:23:21,938
Nadear took good care of you, huh?

266
00:23:22,038 --> 00:23:24,248
She just asked me to reserve a table.

267
00:23:24,778 --> 00:23:25,638
But seriously,

268
00:23:25,658 --> 00:23:27,658
don't you guys ever eat anywhere else?

269
00:23:28,518 --> 00:23:31,058
If we eat here, all three of us make money.

270
00:23:31,268 --> 00:23:32,068
Isn't that good?

271
00:23:33,228 --> 00:23:34,678
Or you don't want it?

272
00:23:34,828 --> 00:23:35,978
Want to pull out your shares, then?

273
00:23:36,258 --> 00:23:37,628
I'm just teasing you.

274
00:23:38,018 --> 00:23:39,588
You only have to say the word,

275
00:23:39,608 --> 00:23:41,418
and I'll reserve a VIP table

276
00:23:41,438 --> 00:23:42,998
with a special menu

277
00:23:43,018 --> 00:23:45,628
for my shareholders, sisters, and family.

278
00:23:46,108 --> 00:23:47,728
Alright, I'll lead the way.

279
00:23:49,638 --> 00:23:50,338
Nadear...

280
00:23:51,728 --> 00:23:53,238
Are your parents here yet?

281
00:23:54,248 --> 00:23:56,028
If I tell you they're already here,

282
00:23:56,138 --> 00:23:58,438
will you stop frowning?

283
00:24:13,998 --> 00:24:15,228
Congratulations, dear.

284
00:24:15,418 --> 00:24:17,248
Time really flies, huh?

285
00:24:17,548 --> 00:24:18,778
Before we know it,

286
00:24:19,038 --> 00:24:21,248
you two have been dating for a decade.

287
00:24:22,408 --> 00:24:23,528
Look at your mother and me.

288
00:24:24,008 --> 00:24:25,528
We've been together for thirty years now.

289
00:24:25,808 --> 00:24:27,118
And that isn't easy, dear.

290
00:24:28,538 --> 00:24:31,518
Then Chris and I will be together
for over thirty years.

291
00:24:32,548 --> 00:24:33,828
Is that true, Chris?

292
00:24:39,728 --> 00:24:41,358
Of course...

293
00:24:42,608 --> 00:24:43,918
Hearing you say that,

294
00:24:43,938 --> 00:24:45,528
I feel relieved.

295
00:24:45,818 --> 00:24:47,548
I have only one daughter

296
00:24:47,578 --> 00:24:49,658
who I love and cherish dearly.

297
00:24:51,478 --> 00:24:52,738
Your father and I

298
00:24:52,758 --> 00:24:54,358
are getting quite old now.

299
00:24:55,108 --> 00:24:57,028
If one day we pass away,

300
00:24:57,458 --> 00:24:59,868
I'm just scared that Nadear would be all alone.

301
00:25:00,968 --> 00:25:01,968
Dearie...

302
00:25:01,988 --> 00:25:04,648
why are you saying sad things
on her anniversary?

303
00:25:04,738 --> 00:25:06,248
Chris already said

304
00:25:06,308 --> 00:25:07,948
they'll be together for over thirty years.

305
00:25:10,238 --> 00:25:11,728
Thank you so much, Chris,

306
00:25:11,898 --> 00:25:13,398
for taking care of Nadear.

307
00:25:14,228 --> 00:25:16,298
I know my daughter

308
00:25:16,318 --> 00:25:17,338
is very stubborn.

309
00:25:17,918 --> 00:25:20,258
But if you're with her,

310
00:25:20,808 --> 00:25:22,728
her father and I can rest easy.

311
00:25:24,198 --> 00:25:26,428
But I'd be even more at ease

312
00:25:26,698 --> 00:25:28,578
if you made it official.

313
00:25:29,998 --> 00:25:32,198
You've been dating for ten years now.

314
00:25:32,498 --> 00:25:34,098
You live in the same house

315
00:25:34,438 --> 00:25:36,438
and work at the same place.

316
00:25:37,338 --> 00:25:39,238
When are you going to get married?

317
00:26:06,738 --> 00:26:08,668
Nan, the influencer at that table

318
00:26:08,688 --> 00:26:09,748
is making a big fuss.

319
00:26:09,768 --> 00:26:11,698
She said I gave her the wrong order,

320
00:26:11,958 --> 00:26:14,498
but I wrote down exactly what she ordered.

321
00:26:14,658 --> 00:26:15,818
Wawah,

322
00:26:15,838 --> 00:26:17,108
if I could split myself in two,

323
00:26:17,128 --> 00:26:18,148
I'd help you with that.

324
00:26:18,448 --> 00:26:19,848
Our head chef is getting complaints

325
00:26:19,868 --> 00:26:21,228
because the food hasn't been served yet.

326
00:26:22,688 --> 00:26:23,228
Alright,

327
00:26:23,248 --> 00:26:24,598
you go calm her down first.

328
00:26:24,618 --> 00:26:27,058
I'll go help out in the kitchen,
then I'll come help you.

329
00:26:27,068 --> 00:26:29,938
If I could do that,
why would I come to you in the first place?!

330
00:26:29,958 --> 00:26:30,818
Wawah,

331
00:26:31,368 --> 00:26:32,718
where is that influencer sitting?

332
00:26:38,798 --> 00:26:39,928
Excuse me,

333
00:26:40,488 --> 00:26:42,828
my waitress told me you got the wrong order?

334
00:26:43,078 --> 00:26:44,888
I ordered baked crab with roe and vermicelli.

335
00:26:45,028 --> 00:26:47,098
But I got baked crab and vermicelli.

336
00:26:47,458 --> 00:26:48,618
I already ate it,

337
00:26:48,638 --> 00:26:50,568
so I knew the crab had no roe in it.

338
00:26:50,648 --> 00:26:52,498
I'd like you to remake the dish.

339
00:26:52,848 --> 00:26:53,848
Because...

340
00:26:54,028 --> 00:26:55,868
I got the wrong dish.

341
00:26:56,198 --> 00:26:58,948
But you really ordered baked crab and vermicelli.

342
00:26:59,308 --> 00:27:00,488
You didn't say, "Crab with roe."

343
00:27:01,248 --> 00:27:03,778
Are you saying I forgot what I said?

344
00:27:06,248 --> 00:27:08,448
Then let me offer you a solution.

345
00:27:08,498 --> 00:27:10,488
We'll check the security footage.

346
00:27:10,518 --> 00:27:12,368
If our waitress is at fault,

347
00:27:12,538 --> 00:27:14,638
we'll take full responsibility.

348
00:27:14,808 --> 00:27:16,838
So you're going to blame the customer, huh?!

349
00:27:17,248 --> 00:27:18,958
You're going to believe her?!

350
00:27:19,268 --> 00:27:20,408
I'm your customer!

351
00:27:22,228 --> 00:27:24,658
I'm sorry for wasting your time.

352
00:27:24,818 --> 00:27:27,638
We'll remake your dish for you.

353
00:27:27,968 --> 00:27:28,978
As an apology,

354
00:27:29,008 --> 00:27:31,898
we won't charge you for this dish.

355
00:27:32,788 --> 00:27:33,848
Excuse me,

356
00:27:33,888 --> 00:27:35,328
are you the owner of this restaurant?

357
00:27:37,138 --> 00:27:38,138
Yes.

358
00:27:38,658 --> 00:27:39,818
No wonder...

359
00:27:40,638 --> 00:27:43,088
you handled things better than other employees.

360
00:27:49,018 --> 00:27:50,938
Why did you listen to the customer?

361
00:27:51,248 --> 00:27:53,018
We didn't even know if it was our fault.

362
00:27:55,108 --> 00:27:57,438
I know you want to do what's right,

363
00:27:58,088 --> 00:27:59,588
and you don't want to hurt her feelings.

364
00:28:00,848 --> 00:28:03,238
But trying to find out the truth
is a waste of time.

365
00:28:03,948 --> 00:28:05,998
And if the customer is dissatisfied,

366
00:28:06,088 --> 00:28:08,758
she might write a bad review,
which would make things worse.

367
00:28:09,918 --> 00:28:11,618
Even though we're not wrong?

368
00:28:12,868 --> 00:28:16,258
Taking the blame
is another way to resolve an issue.

369
00:28:20,008 --> 00:28:22,778
So you think I can't handle this on my own?

370
00:28:23,698 --> 00:28:25,248
This is my restaurant as well.

371
00:28:25,298 --> 00:28:27,738
But you haven't worked in a long time.

372
00:28:27,998 --> 00:28:29,748
You wouldn't understand the customers.

373
00:28:31,648 --> 00:28:32,848
Trust me, alright?

374
00:28:33,578 --> 00:28:36,018
Don't let this ruin our special day.

375
00:28:36,648 --> 00:28:37,828
Let's go back to lunch.

376
00:28:38,148 --> 00:28:39,428
Mom and Dad are waiting.

377
00:28:43,578 --> 00:28:44,948
I can only go, can't I?

378
00:28:48,498 --> 00:28:50,478
[Happy 10th Anniversary,
Chris and Nadear]

379
00:28:50,498 --> 00:28:51,588
- Mm, so delicious.
- Is it good?

380
00:28:51,608 --> 00:28:52,658
There's salted egg.

381
00:28:53,258 --> 00:28:54,258
Cholesterol, huh?

382
00:28:58,108 --> 00:28:59,428
You won't be lonely anymore.

383
00:29:00,348 --> 00:29:01,948
Come live with me, little rose.

384
00:29:02,178 --> 00:29:04,238
How did you know it's a rose plant?

385
00:29:05,048 --> 00:29:06,048
Have you grown one before?

386
00:29:06,818 --> 00:29:08,248
I did when I was younger,

387
00:29:08,268 --> 00:29:08,898
but...

388
00:29:09,498 --> 00:29:11,138
after I moved, I didn't have any.

389
00:29:12,828 --> 00:29:14,548
Do you think it'll survive?

390
00:29:16,528 --> 00:29:18,138
It depends on...

391
00:29:19,708 --> 00:29:21,338
how you treat it.

392
00:29:22,838 --> 00:29:24,448
Treating a plant

393
00:29:24,628 --> 00:29:26,168
is like treating a person.

394
00:29:27,448 --> 00:29:28,618
If you don't take good care of it,

395
00:29:29,038 --> 00:29:30,638
don't water

396
00:29:31,298 --> 00:29:32,508
or cherish it,

397
00:29:34,118 --> 00:29:35,618
it won't work out.

398
00:29:39,998 --> 00:29:42,368
But since this is the rose plant you saved,

399
00:29:51,498 --> 00:29:52,668
I'll work it out.

400
00:29:55,348 --> 00:29:56,638
Because I want to stay close.

401
00:30:06,088 --> 00:30:07,618
The rose plant would be happy to hear that.

402
00:30:09,048 --> 00:30:10,518
You're the one who should be happy.

403
00:30:11,078 --> 00:30:12,748
The one I want to stay close to

404
00:30:13,298 --> 00:30:14,518
is you, Chris.

405
00:30:51,238 --> 00:30:52,688
Can't you do this for my parents

406
00:30:52,708 --> 00:30:55,138
every once in a while?

407
00:30:55,448 --> 00:30:57,148
Why did you have to run away?

408
00:30:58,088 --> 00:30:59,848
Did you know I had to lie to them

409
00:30:59,868 --> 00:31:02,618
that you were feeling sick,
so you couldn't see them off to their car?

410
00:31:03,778 --> 00:31:05,938
You're good at lying anyway, aren't you?

411
00:31:06,728 --> 00:31:08,428
Just like when you lied to our customer.

412
00:31:10,238 --> 00:31:11,758
Is this really your excuse

413
00:31:11,778 --> 00:31:13,938
for not seeing my parents off?

414
00:31:15,338 --> 00:31:16,338
I'm not making excuses.

415
00:31:17,798 --> 00:31:19,758
But you're being sarcastic.

416
00:31:21,128 --> 00:31:22,528
That's not okay...

417
00:31:23,828 --> 00:31:25,248
Then what can I do?

418
00:31:25,748 --> 00:31:26,688
Can I tell you the truth?

419
00:31:26,708 --> 00:31:28,258
I don't want to see your parents off

420
00:31:28,278 --> 00:31:29,468
because I feel ashamed.

421
00:31:30,128 --> 00:31:32,328
I can't face your parents.

422
00:31:32,788 --> 00:31:35,008
I can't lie to them any longer.

423
00:31:36,098 --> 00:31:36,938
Chris...

424
00:31:37,308 --> 00:31:38,958
I can't take this anymore.

425
00:31:39,348 --> 00:31:42,418
Pretending we're in love for your parents

426
00:31:42,748 --> 00:31:44,438
won't put their minds at ease,

427
00:31:44,458 --> 00:31:46,328
so you can live your life freely.

428
00:31:47,538 --> 00:31:48,538
Do you know why?

429
00:31:49,858 --> 00:31:51,428
Because if we're still together,

430
00:31:52,488 --> 00:31:54,018
we'll always fight.

431
00:31:54,258 --> 00:31:55,988
Do you have someone else?

432
00:31:56,728 --> 00:31:58,248
Why shouldn't I?

433
00:32:00,728 --> 00:32:02,228
We broke up a long time ago.

434
00:32:09,638 --> 00:32:13,008
[Third Person]

435
00:32:14,638 --> 00:32:18,028
[Third Person]

436
00:32:39,158 --> 00:32:40,558
I'm sorry...

437
00:32:41,638 --> 00:32:43,558
I said mean things to you today.

438
00:32:46,218 --> 00:32:47,518
I'll change.

439
00:32:48,938 --> 00:32:50,398
It won't happen again.

440
00:32:55,928 --> 00:32:57,518
Will you forgive me?

441
00:32:58,038 --> 00:32:59,908
Please, Chris...?

442
00:33:02,778 --> 00:33:03,817
Okay, okay.

443
00:33:03,818 --> 00:33:04,618
Alright.

444
00:33:06,238 --> 00:33:08,678
I love you because you're so kind.

445
00:33:43,448 --> 00:33:44,778
I'm sorry.

446
00:33:45,498 --> 00:33:47,948
I know your body is rejecting this,

447
00:33:48,918 --> 00:33:50,618
but I just want to hug you.

448
00:33:57,438 --> 00:33:58,758
I'll wait...

449
00:34:00,098 --> 00:34:02,598
until you feel better.

450
00:34:03,408 --> 00:34:05,418
Until we can hug each other.

451
00:34:09,528 --> 00:34:11,258
But it's been four years now, Nadear.

452
00:34:11,798 --> 00:34:13,768
No matter how long I have to wait,

453
00:34:14,158 --> 00:34:15,708
I won't give up.

454
00:34:16,528 --> 00:34:19,398
I'll make you want to hug me.

455
00:34:22,378 --> 00:34:24,598
And don't go hugging anyone else before me.

456
00:34:28,768 --> 00:34:30,978
But you couldn't do that, could you?

457
00:34:31,958 --> 00:34:33,417
You can't even stand

458
00:34:33,418 --> 00:34:35,068
touching anyone else.

459
00:34:37,758 --> 00:34:39,328
Your past trauma

460
00:34:40,168 --> 00:34:42,418
made your body reject physical touch.

461
00:34:43,638 --> 00:34:46,598
It's a defense mechanism
caused by your trauma.

462
00:34:48,078 --> 00:34:50,768
If you heal from that trauma,

463
00:34:51,338 --> 00:34:52,268
your body

464
00:34:52,918 --> 00:34:54,757
will slowly stop rejecting physical contact.

465
00:34:54,758 --> 00:34:57,348
What if it suddenly stopped rejecting?

466
00:34:57,918 --> 00:34:59,348
Can you touch Nadear now?

467
00:35:01,768 --> 00:35:03,198
Not Nadear,

468
00:35:05,198 --> 00:35:07,328
but a woman I met by accident.

469
00:35:17,038 --> 00:35:19,038
When we were close,

470
00:35:20,728 --> 00:35:22,408
I didn't feel uncomfortable.

471
00:35:23,848 --> 00:35:27,018
I didn't feel awkward like
when I was with Nadear...

472
00:35:27,408 --> 00:35:29,758
or with any other woman.

473
00:35:29,908 --> 00:35:33,508
What did you feel
when you were close to her?

474
00:35:34,298 --> 00:35:35,488
I wanted to stop,

475
00:35:37,138 --> 00:35:38,268
but I couldn't.

476
00:35:39,298 --> 00:35:40,778
I couldn't stop myself.

477
00:35:42,518 --> 00:35:43,788
Do you like her?

478
00:35:44,958 --> 00:35:46,828
I tried not to have any feelings for her.

479
00:35:47,218 --> 00:35:48,878
Then what will you do next?

480
00:35:52,318 --> 00:35:54,068
What can I do?

481
00:35:54,808 --> 00:35:57,247
You know I still have to live with Nadear.

482
00:35:57,248 --> 00:35:58,998
But you two already broke up.

483
00:35:59,138 --> 00:36:01,298
I can't tell anyone that, Doctor.

484
00:36:02,018 --> 00:36:03,428
From an outsider's perspective,

485
00:36:04,198 --> 00:36:05,818
we'd still have to be together.

486
00:36:06,488 --> 00:36:08,928
I just don't want her to

487
00:36:09,278 --> 00:36:11,538
get tangled up in this mess.

488
00:36:12,498 --> 00:36:13,888
Let me ask you something.

489
00:36:14,178 --> 00:36:16,388
If you could touch Nadear,

490
00:36:16,638 --> 00:36:18,018
would anything change?

491
00:36:22,258 --> 00:36:23,327
Before we broke up,

492
00:36:23,328 --> 00:36:26,708
I already told Nadear that this
isn't about physical contact.

493
00:36:27,418 --> 00:36:29,338
Even if we'd had sex,

494
00:36:30,178 --> 00:36:31,678
we would've broken up anyway.

495
00:36:33,498 --> 00:36:35,658
Nadear and I really aren't compatible.

496
00:36:37,698 --> 00:36:38,928
Then...

497
00:36:39,758 --> 00:36:41,388
why don't you talk to Nadear about this?

498
00:36:42,178 --> 00:36:46,018
If that woman can help you feel better,

499
00:36:46,618 --> 00:36:48,028
Nadear will understand.

500
00:36:48,498 --> 00:36:49,998
And what if she doesn't?

501
00:36:50,558 --> 00:36:51,688
I know

502
00:36:52,278 --> 00:36:54,028
that you feel bad for Nadear,

503
00:36:55,818 --> 00:36:57,748
but I want you to be happy.

504
00:36:58,378 --> 00:36:59,738
This is your life.

505
00:37:00,718 --> 00:37:03,848
Are you going to let guilt
stop you from being happy?

506
00:37:40,018 --> 00:37:40,718
Sun.

507
00:37:42,438 --> 00:37:42,868
Yes?

508
00:37:43,358 --> 00:37:44,058
I'm sorry,

509
00:37:44,058 --> 00:37:44,998
I got the wrong person.

510
00:37:45,678 --> 00:37:46,818
Oh, okay.

511
00:38:21,058 --> 00:38:22,008
Thank you.

512
00:38:25,338 --> 00:38:26,658
You broke your promise.

513
00:38:27,128 --> 00:38:28,478
Didn't you say you'd
run here yesterday?

514
00:38:29,578 --> 00:38:30,048
What?

515
00:38:30,258 --> 00:38:31,708
Did you run here yesterday?

516
00:38:32,398 --> 00:38:34,548
I probably... assumed

517
00:38:35,298 --> 00:38:36,338
that we'd meet here.

518
00:38:38,238 --> 00:38:39,338
I'm sorry...

519
00:38:39,608 --> 00:38:41,338
I had errands yesterday.

520
00:38:42,368 --> 00:38:43,148
What if tomorrow...

521
00:38:43,149 --> 00:38:44,218
I'm not free tomorrow.

522
00:38:49,288 --> 00:38:50,748
But I'm free today.

523
00:38:52,218 --> 00:38:53,858
Are you good at gardening?

524
00:39:00,818 --> 00:39:02,808
Didn't you say you knew
how to grow plants?

525
00:39:03,118 --> 00:39:04,558
You said you took care of a rose plant.

526
00:39:05,318 --> 00:39:06,797
That was a long time ago,

527
00:39:06,798 --> 00:39:08,558
and my father helped me too.

528
00:39:08,998 --> 00:39:10,758
If I have to do it alone,

529
00:39:11,058 --> 00:39:12,758
I don't know if it'll work out.

530
00:39:15,818 --> 00:39:16,858
Then...

531
00:39:17,888 --> 00:39:19,438
Let's learn together.

532
00:39:21,238 --> 00:39:22,848
Didn't you say you knew how to grow plants?

533
00:39:25,288 --> 00:39:27,048
Well, if I said I didn't know how to grow plants,

534
00:39:27,358 --> 00:39:28,688
would I get to come with you?

535
00:39:30,218 --> 00:39:31,317
You don't have to lie

536
00:39:31,318 --> 00:39:33,648
to come with me.

537
00:39:34,218 --> 00:39:37,018
You can just say you want to come,
and I'll let you come with me.

538
00:39:44,168 --> 00:39:45,158
Hello.

539
00:39:45,568 --> 00:39:47,178
What plant would you like?

540
00:39:49,598 --> 00:39:51,807
I'll get the soil and the rest of the plants

541
00:39:51,808 --> 00:39:52,808
for you.

542
00:39:52,958 --> 00:39:53,528
Thank you.

543
00:39:53,528 --> 00:39:54,528
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

544
00:39:56,488 --> 00:39:58,428
I thought you only wanted to grow roses,

545
00:39:58,568 --> 00:39:59,888
but you wanted to be a cook as well?

546
00:40:00,808 --> 00:40:03,868
I've wanted to pick ingredients
straight from the garden for a while now.

547
00:40:04,128 --> 00:40:05,428
- Mm...
- So...

548
00:40:05,848 --> 00:40:07,748
Don't you want to grow something as well, Chris?

549
00:40:08,938 --> 00:40:11,008
I'm not that into growing plants,

550
00:40:12,018 --> 00:40:14,038
but I like the smell of petrichor.

551
00:40:14,238 --> 00:40:15,628
It feels refreshing.

552
00:40:15,968 --> 00:40:16,858
Then that means...

553
00:40:17,118 --> 00:40:18,578
you like the smell of bacteria.

554
00:40:19,378 --> 00:40:19,878
Hm?

555
00:40:22,688 --> 00:40:24,137
The smell of petrichor

556
00:40:24,138 --> 00:40:27,138
comes from plants' natural oils.

557
00:40:27,368 --> 00:40:28,798
When it rains,

558
00:40:28,948 --> 00:40:31,297
these oils mix with chemicals in the soil,

559
00:40:31,298 --> 00:40:33,418
especially geosmin

560
00:40:34,278 --> 00:40:35,518
from bacteria,

561
00:40:36,298 --> 00:40:38,838
creating the refreshing smell you like.

562
00:40:38,998 --> 00:40:41,838
They say this chemical can make you feel calm

563
00:40:42,158 --> 00:40:43,718
and relieve stress.

564
00:40:46,858 --> 00:40:48,378
You're such a nerd.

565
00:40:49,278 --> 00:40:50,758
Do you like nerds, then?

566
00:41:25,418 --> 00:41:26,598
Are you alright?

567
00:41:29,178 --> 00:41:30,478
We ran through the rain yesterday,

568
00:41:30,658 --> 00:41:31,788
and today we ran through the sprinklers.

569
00:41:32,218 --> 00:41:33,358
How eventful.

570
00:41:34,218 --> 00:41:36,018
But this shouldn't have happened.

571
00:41:36,258 --> 00:41:37,497
They could see that we were there,

572
00:41:37,498 --> 00:41:38,978
so why did they turn on the sprinklers?

573
00:41:40,258 --> 00:41:41,108
I'll talk to them.

574
00:41:41,738 --> 00:41:42,608
Chris.

575
00:41:46,608 --> 00:41:47,778
Do you smell that?

576
00:41:51,568 --> 00:41:52,218
Mm.

577
00:41:52,918 --> 00:41:53,698
The smell...

578
00:41:53,698 --> 00:41:54,688
of bacteria.

579
00:41:55,798 --> 00:41:57,608
It actually helps relieve stress, huh?

580
00:42:01,738 --> 00:42:03,968
It's not because of the petrichor, though.

581
00:42:05,178 --> 00:42:06,618
Are you saying it's because of me?

582
00:42:09,098 --> 00:42:10,738
You're quite a narcissist, huh?

583
00:42:12,278 --> 00:42:13,338
Am I wrong, then?

584
00:42:15,168 --> 00:42:16,698
If it weren't for you,

585
00:42:17,618 --> 00:42:19,858
I would've been so stressed
my head would have exploded.

586
00:42:22,298 --> 00:42:24,068
I defused the bomb for you,

587
00:42:24,408 --> 00:42:25,998
so you don't have to be angry anymore.

588
00:42:26,898 --> 00:42:29,008
They probably didn't mean to make
their customers wet.

589
00:42:32,008 --> 00:42:33,808
How can you be so optimistic?

590
00:42:36,248 --> 00:42:38,338
Maybe it's because
I've been through terrible things.

591
00:42:40,018 --> 00:42:42,658
If I don't look at the bright side,

592
00:42:43,648 --> 00:42:46,018
I might not be able to move forward.

593
00:42:51,498 --> 00:42:52,818
Let's get our plants.

594
00:43:00,738 --> 00:43:04,218
[Third Person]

595
00:43:05,949 --> 00:43:09,229
[Third Person]

596
00:43:12,089 --> 00:43:13,418
Take a shower right away

597
00:43:13,419 --> 00:43:14,539
before you get sick.

598
00:43:16,619 --> 00:43:17,499
It's funny

599
00:43:17,500 --> 00:43:19,319
how we got wet on different days.

600
00:43:20,029 --> 00:43:22,679
But it won't be funny if you get sick.

601
00:43:23,169 --> 00:43:24,529
I won't be.

602
00:43:27,139 --> 00:43:28,099
I'll take a shower now.

603
00:43:35,929 --> 00:43:36,639
Hey!

604
00:43:37,699 --> 00:43:38,909
What're you doing?

605
00:43:41,219 --> 00:43:43,259
Didn't you tell me to
take a shower right away?

606
00:43:44,129 --> 00:43:46,259
Well, you don't have to rush that much.

607
00:43:53,859 --> 00:43:55,369
You have to survive

608
00:43:55,709 --> 00:43:57,029
so we can be together for a long time.

609
00:43:59,939 --> 00:44:02,249
I want to see beautiful roses from you too.

610
00:44:19,899 --> 00:44:21,048
If you're done unwrapping,

611
00:44:21,049 --> 00:44:22,559
you can put it there.

612
00:44:27,909 --> 00:44:28,529
Oh!

613
00:44:29,709 --> 00:44:30,469
Hey,

614
00:44:30,470 --> 00:44:31,509
get back inside.

615
00:44:38,909 --> 00:44:40,229
What is it, Chris?

616
00:44:45,859 --> 00:44:47,869
Someone might take photos of you.

617
00:44:48,069 --> 00:44:50,089
Phone cameras have such powerful zoom nowadays.

618
00:44:53,769 --> 00:44:55,369
Just say you're worried about me.

619
00:44:56,059 --> 00:44:57,949
No need to explain this much.

620
00:45:10,689 --> 00:45:12,189
Don't worry anymore.

621
00:45:16,179 --> 00:45:17,819
No one can see me in this room

622
00:45:18,909 --> 00:45:20,459
except the one I want them to.

623
00:45:25,129 --> 00:45:26,699
I'll have to save the plants.

624
00:45:41,469 --> 00:45:42,219
Chris.

625
00:45:43,129 --> 00:45:43,859
Oh!

626
00:45:45,659 --> 00:45:47,409
You've been out here for a while now.

627
00:45:47,769 --> 00:45:49,229
Is there something on your mind?

628
00:45:49,669 --> 00:45:50,919
Should we head back inside?

629
00:45:51,569 --> 00:45:52,748
I'm fine outside.

630
00:45:52,749 --> 00:45:54,469
I like looking at the plants.

631
00:45:56,689 --> 00:45:57,719
Is that so?

632
00:45:58,819 --> 00:45:59,789
Yeah.

633
00:46:04,779 --> 00:46:06,239
Then let me introduce you to them.

634
00:46:06,889 --> 00:46:08,479
This is Ri.

635
00:46:08,949 --> 00:46:10,478
If it sprouts more leaves,

636
00:46:10,479 --> 00:46:12,749
I'll promote it to Ri-ri.

637
00:46:14,109 --> 00:46:15,219
And this is...

638
00:46:15,649 --> 00:46:16,489
Li.

639
00:46:17,749 --> 00:46:20,219
If it grows a bit more, I'll promote it too.

640
00:46:23,869 --> 00:46:25,039
Promote it to Li-li?

641
00:46:25,809 --> 00:46:26,879
Yeah.

642
00:46:28,909 --> 00:46:30,509
And these are...

643
00:46:31,539 --> 00:46:32,929
Oo-oo-oo.

644
00:46:35,249 --> 00:46:36,599
Oo-oo-oo?

645
00:46:38,749 --> 00:46:39,599
Yeah.

646
00:46:39,869 --> 00:46:41,349
That's a cute name.

647
00:46:57,569 --> 00:46:58,618
Make yourself at home.

648
00:46:58,619 --> 00:46:59,859
I'll wait inside.

649
00:47:09,479 --> 00:47:11,479
[Nadear]

650
00:47:25,389 --> 00:47:26,589
Jeen...

651
00:47:28,939 --> 00:47:31,209
Chris has never been like this before.

652
00:47:33,309 --> 00:47:35,729
I don't know what to do anymore.

653
00:47:36,649 --> 00:47:37,789
What happened, Nadear?

654
00:47:39,849 --> 00:47:42,729
I feel like I'm about to lose her.

655
00:47:44,939 --> 00:47:47,119
Can you help me, Jeen?

656
00:47:48,309 --> 00:47:50,579
I can't lose her.

657
00:47:50,979 --> 00:47:54,279
I want Chris to love me like she used to.

658
00:49:31,009 --> 00:49:32,499
Are you a dancer?

659
00:49:35,229 --> 00:49:36,859
Is that an insult?

660
00:49:37,749 --> 00:49:38,929
No.

661
00:49:39,309 --> 00:49:39,889
Well...

662
00:49:39,890 --> 00:49:41,749
You seem to enjoy music.

663
00:49:43,069 --> 00:49:44,499
Are you a DJ?

664
00:49:46,009 --> 00:49:46,629
Wrong.

665
00:49:47,509 --> 00:49:48,669
Then...

666
00:49:48,929 --> 00:49:49,699
a model?

667
00:49:54,099 --> 00:49:55,379
Try again.

668
00:49:55,939 --> 00:49:57,779
You know what my job is.

669
00:50:04,109 --> 00:50:05,239
Are you a doctor?

670
00:50:06,649 --> 00:50:07,699
You're smart.

671
00:50:08,899 --> 00:50:10,229
No, you are.

672
00:50:12,309 --> 00:50:14,828
I don't really work
as a doctor much anymore.

673
00:50:14,829 --> 00:50:16,629
I'm more on the management side now.

674
00:50:17,429 --> 00:50:19,479
I co-own a clinic with my friend.

675
00:50:21,229 --> 00:50:22,309
Then...

676
00:50:22,859 --> 00:50:25,408
can you look at my face for me, Doc?

677
00:50:25,409 --> 00:50:27,259
Are there any adjustments needed?

678
00:50:40,019 --> 00:50:41,589
You're already pretty.

679
00:50:42,669 --> 00:50:44,139
Your skin is glowing.

680
00:50:46,699 --> 00:50:48,899
Your features are well-balanced.

681
00:50:51,579 --> 00:50:53,489
Your under-eyes are full and plump.

682
00:50:54,989 --> 00:50:56,699
No need for fillers.

683
00:50:58,059 --> 00:50:59,469
Your chin...

684
00:50:59,659 --> 00:51:01,269
is naturally beautiful.

685
00:51:03,619 --> 00:51:05,229
As for your lips...

686
00:51:06,969 --> 00:51:07,899
very kissable.

687
00:51:31,299 --> 00:51:33,249
It's alright if you can't hug me.

688
00:51:34,229 --> 00:51:37,229
I just want you to stay by my side.

689
00:51:42,689 --> 00:51:43,469
What's wrong?

690
00:51:49,349 --> 00:51:51,219
I was in a car accident several years ago.

691
00:51:54,819 --> 00:51:56,029
Does it still hurt?

692
00:52:03,289 --> 00:52:06,409
My doctor said the accident made me
reject physical contact.

693
00:52:08,209 --> 00:52:11,089
It's a defense mechanism in response to trauma.

694
00:52:14,299 --> 00:52:15,569
The trauma here?

695
00:52:22,699 --> 00:52:25,439
I thought physical touch
could help you recover.

696
00:53:11,809 --> 00:53:14,779
I don't want you to be
in this terrible relationship.

697
00:53:14,909 --> 00:53:16,879
Follow your heart, Chris.

698
00:53:17,249 --> 00:53:19,639
You make the person you're with feel seen.

699
00:53:19,819 --> 00:53:20,799
That's the reason

700
00:53:20,969 --> 00:53:22,749
I want to be your friend.

701
00:53:24,099 --> 00:53:25,379
Who gave you this?

702
00:53:26,499 --> 00:53:27,279
A friend.

703
00:53:27,869 --> 00:53:29,498
I don't want to see you in pain

704
00:53:29,499 --> 00:53:31,499
or see you sad anymore,

705
00:53:32,289 --> 00:53:34,219
because I love you!

706
00:53:34,509 --> 00:53:35,979
Am I wrong for that?

707
00:53:38,309 --> 00:53:40,119
Friends don't kiss, do they?

708
00:53:55,099 --> 00:54:05,068
♫The rain keeps splashing beneath our cover,♫

709
00:54:05,069 --> 00:54:10,228
♫Once it was a special place for two lovers♫

710
00:54:10,229 --> 00:54:14,498
♫There was never enough room for the third♫

711
00:54:14,499 --> 00:54:20,218
♫Now, the rain soaks our hearts together♫

712
00:54:20,219 --> 00:54:29,789
♫The question that's trapped in my heart♫

713
00:54:29,809 --> 00:54:35,108
♫Maybe it's time for you to do your part♫

714
00:54:35,109 --> 00:54:39,418
♫Choose the one your heart truly desires♫

715
00:54:39,419 --> 00:54:48,249
♫Before the last raindrop falls,
don't make me shed another tear♫

716
00:54:48,779 --> 00:54:57,769
♫Before the last raindrop falls,
don't make me shed another tear♫
